{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed dwelling, by virtue of its scale, would fail to provide an adequately sized communal living space which would be narrow and have poor natural daylight. This would present a cramped living environment and a sub-standard quality of accommodation contrary to:DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Policy D4, D6 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMD1&nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)",
    "The bulk, mass, scale, siting and design of the proposed dwelling would present a discordant feature to the terrace row, appearing significantly narrower than the rest of the dwellings appearing more akin to a subordinate side extension than a dwelling in its own right. The proposal fails to incorporate the key distinctive architectural features of the terrace row disrupting the uniformity, rhythm and visual coherence of the terrace row, harmful to the character of the area. As such, this is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies D1 and D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1, DMD5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed off-street car parking arrangement would involve the installation of a new crossover resulting in the loss of on-street parking, further increasing parking stress in the area. This is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraph 116 of the&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (MHCLG, December 2024)Policy T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT 3 of the&nbsp;London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s&nbsp;Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
